---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

// MCP discovery page: how AI agents and MCP clients connect to the Pour Picks
// database. Human-readable and indexable; the machine-readable surface is
// the MCP endpoint itself plus llms.txt.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pour Picks MCP Server — Bourbon Data for AI Agents"
  description="Connect Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, or any MCP client to the Pour Picks bourbon database: search 4,700+ bottles, compare, find cheaper alternatives, and get pour recommendations."
  path="/mcp"
>
  <main class="page">
    <h1>Pour Picks for AI agents (MCP)</h1>

    <p>The Pour Picks MCP server gives AI assistants read-only access to our bourbon &amp; whiskey database: 4,700+ bottles with structured tasting profiles, proof, price, pairings, and community ratings. Ask your AI for bourbon recommendations, bourbon comparisons, bottles similar to ones you love, or a cheaper alternative with the same flavor profile &mdash; and it can answer from real catalog data instead of guessing.</p>

    <h2>Connect in one minute</h2>

    <p><strong>Claude</strong> &mdash; one click, then confirm the connector:</p>
    <p>
      <a
        class="cta"
        href="https://claude.ai/customize/connectors?modal=add-custom-connector&connectorName=Pour%20Picks&connectorUrl=https%3A%2F%2Fnqnigdqkcvrziwcbgily.supabase.co%2Ffunctions%2Fv1%2Fmcp"
        rel="noopener">Connect to Claude</a>
    </p>

    <p><strong>Claude Desktop</strong> (and other clients that launch local servers) &mdash; add to your MCP config:</p>
    <pre is:raw><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pour-picks": { "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "pour-picks-mcp"] }
  }
}</code></pre>
    <p><strong>Remote clients</strong> (web agents, Cursor, anything that takes a URL) &mdash; use the hosted endpoint, no install or API key:</p>
    <pre><code>https://nqnigdqkcvrziwcbgily.supabase.co/functions/v1/mcp</code></pre>

    <h2>What tools does the Pour Picks MCP server provide?</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>search_bottles</code></td><td>Search bourbons by name, category, price, and proof</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>get_bottle</code></td><td>Full tasting profile, price, and ratings for one bottle</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>find_similar</code></td><td>Bottles with a similar flavor profile</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>find_cheaper_alternative</code></td><td>Same style, lower price</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>get_recommendations</code></td><td>Personalized picks from flavors, budget, and occasion</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>compare_bottles</code></td><td>Side-by-side comparison</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>trending_bottles</code></td><td>What collectors are adding to cellars right now</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>pour_tonight_suggestion</code></td><td>What to pour based on mood, occasion, and season</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>What can an AI answer with it?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>&ldquo;What bourbon is similar to Eagle Rare but easier to find?&rdquo;</li>
      <li>&ldquo;Recommend a bourbon under $60 with vanilla, oak, and caramel notes.&rdquo;</li>
      <li>&ldquo;What tastes like Blanton’s without the price tag?&rdquo;</li>
      <li>&ldquo;What should I pour on a cold night?&rdquo;</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Access, privacy, and attribution</h2>
    <p>All tools are read-only and public &mdash; no account, API key, or authentication is required. Requests are rate-limited to 60 calls per minute. Every response includes source attribution and data freshness dates; quote freely with attribution to Pour Picks (pourpicks.app). Anonymous usage telemetry (tool name, arguments, client name, timing) is logged to operate the service and purged after 90 days; no user identity or conversation content is collected.</p>

    <h2>For developers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>npm package: <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/pour-picks-mcp">pour-picks-mcp</a></li>
      <li>GitHub (README, examples): <a href="https://github.com/bguillow-rgb/pour-picks-mcp">bguillow-rgb/pour-picks-mcp</a></li>
      <li>Official MCP registry: <code>io.github.bguillow-rgb/pour-picks</code></li>
      <li>Smithery listing: <a href="https://smithery.ai/servers/bguillow/pour-picks">smithery.ai/servers/bguillow/pour-picks</a></li>
    </ul>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
